\chapter{Development stages}

Each stage is an \emph{edition} of this book: at its boundary everything
tangles, builds green, and reads complete for what exists. No stage begins
before the previous one is proven --- software is evolutionary, and every
stage stands on ground already solid.

\section{Stage 1 --- the walking skeleton}

<The thinnest vertical slice that tangles to a RUNNING system. It must touch
every Stage-1 concept, however thinly: a skeleton that skips a concept proves
nothing about the architecture. Say what running it demonstrates.>

\paragraph{Proven when} <the observable fact that closes this stage: a command
runs, an invariant holds under test, a round trip returns the right value.>

